{% block art_body %}

<div class="callout key">
  <span class="co-h">{{ t('Bottom line', '核心结论') }}</span>
  {{ t('Meta is the market&rsquo;s freshest rerating story, and the comparison to Google&rsquo;s Q4-2025 run is real — but it conflates two different jobs. The stock that <em>absorbs capital during</em> the coming midterm-window correction and the stock that <em>reprices out of its low</em> are not the same stock. The tape has already cast Apple as this cycle&rsquo;s hiding place; Meta is auditioning for the <em>recovery</em> lead, and its Google-moment is scheduled for the October window — after the capex fear and the dilution event flush out, not before. Nvidia is the coiled rebound, not the shelter. Tesla isn&rsquo;t in this contest. And Washington is genuinely long the AI trade — literally, in equity stakes — but it is not picking the haven: the Fed and the cycle outrank the White House, and everything the administration telegraphs gets front-run.',
        'Meta 是当下市场最新鲜的重估故事，与谷歌 2025 年四季度那轮行情的类比也确有其事——但它混淆了两份不同的工作。在即将到来的中期选举窗口调整中<em>吸纳资金</em>的股票，与从低点<em>完成重估</em>的股票，不是同一只。盘面已经把 Apple 选为本轮周期的藏身之所；Meta 试镜的是<em>复苏</em>阶段的主角，它的「谷歌时刻」排在十月窗口——在资本开支恐惧与稀释事件冲洗干净之后，而不是之前。Nvidia 是蓄势的反弹弹簧，不是避风港。Tesla 根本不在这场选角里。而华盛顿确实做多 AI 交易——甚至直接持有股权——但它并没有在挑选避险股：美联储与周期的权力高于白宫，且政府预告的一切都会被市场抢跑。') }}
</div>

<div class="statband">
