  <div class="stat" style="--sc:#d23f3f;"><span class="sv dn">&minus;21.6%</span><span class="sl">{{ t('META during that quarter&rsquo;s QQQ drawdown (Oct 29&ndash;Nov 20) — the worst megacap. The haven candidate was the worst performer last time.', '同季 QQQ 回撤期（10月29日&ndash;11月20日）META 的表现 —— 七巨头中最差。上一次压力测试里，这位「避险候选人」垫底。') }}</span></div>
  <div class="stat" style="--sc:#5b8def;"><span class="sv">77%</span><span class="sl">{{ t('AAPL&rsquo;s beat-rate vs QQQ on down days since Jun 1 — the tape&rsquo;s actual haven vote', '6月1日以来 QQQ 下跌日中 AAPL 跑赢的比例 —— 盘面真实的避险投票') }}</span></div>
  <div class="stat" style="--sc:#e0973a;"><span class="sv dn">$0</span><span class="sl">{{ t('Meta buybacks in Q1 2026 (vs $12.75B a year ago), with a ~$64B equity raise under consideration — the anti-haven mechanic', '2026年一季度 Meta 回购金额（去年同期 127.5 亿美元），且约 640 亿美元股权融资在酝酿中 —— 反避险的资本机制') }}</span></div>
  <div class="stat" style="--sc:#c77dff;"><span class="sv">Oct</span><span class="sl">{{ t('Modal month of midterm-year lows (2022, 2014, 2002, 1998, 1990, 1966) — where Meta&rsquo;s real window sits', '中期选举年低点的众数月份（2022、2014、2002、1998、1990、1966）—— Meta 真正的窗口所在') }}</span></div>
</div>

<h2 id="answer"><span class="num">1</span>{{ t('The ten-second answer', '十秒答案') }}</h2>

<div class="callout lead"><span class="co-h">{{ t('In plain English', '通俗版') }}</span>
{{ t('You asked: will Meta become the safe place big money hides, the way Google was last autumn — and which of Meta, Nvidia, Apple and Tesla has been picked to weather the next selloff? Short version: money <em>hides</em> in Apple and, to a lesser degree, Google. Money <em>redeploys into</em> Meta, Nvidia and Microsoft at the October low. Meta&rsquo;s big rerating is real but it needs proof it hasn&rsquo;t printed yet — and it is more likely to arrive <em>through</em> the scary dip than instead of it. Nobody in Washington picked any of this; they just built tailwinds and are riding the same trade.',
     '你问的是：Meta 会不会变成大资金的藏身之所，就像去年秋天的谷歌——以及 Meta、Nvidia、Apple、Tesla 里，哪一只被选中来扛过下一轮抛售？简版答案：资金<em>藏</em>在 Apple、其次是谷歌；到十月低点，资金<em>重新部署</em>进 Meta、Nvidia 和微软。Meta 的大重估是真的，但它需要尚未打印出来的证据——而且它更可能<em>穿过</em>那次吓人的下跌到来，而不是替代它。华盛顿没有钦点任何一只股票；他们只是修好了顺风道，然后和市场坐在同一笔交易里。') }}
</div>

<table class="data scn">
  <tr><th>{{ t('Candidate', '候选人') }}</th><th>{{ t('During the correction (now &rarr; Oct)', '调整期内（当下 &rarr; 10月）') }}</th><th>{{ t('Out of the low (Oct &rarr; 2027)', '低点之后（10月 &rarr; 2027）') }}</th></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>META</strong></td><td>{{ t('Two-way volatility, not shelter. The July 29 print is a binary. Do not confuse a rerating candidate with a bunker.', '双向剧烈波动，不是掩体。7月29日财报是二元事件。别把重估候选人当防空洞。') }}</td><td><strong>{{ t('#1 asymmetry.', '不对称性第一。') }}</strong> {{ t('The Google-analog trade, properly timed: buy the capex-fear flush, tranche discipline.', '正确择时的谷歌类比交易：买资本开支恐惧的冲洗，分批纪律。') }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>AAPL</strong></td><td><strong>{{ t('The anointed haven.', '受膏的避风港。') }}</strong> {{ t('The tape already voted. But you are paying a ~53% premium to its own decade average for shelter.', '盘面已投票。但为这份庇护，你付的是较其十年均值溢价约 53% 的价格。') }}</td><td>{{ t('The donor. Haven flows unwind into the recovery; least upside of the five.', '献血者。避险资金在复苏中撤出；五者中上行空间最小。') }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>NVDA</strong></td><td>{{ t('Falls with its complex — less than memory, but it falls. A $118B buyback is a floor, not a shield.', '与所属板块同跌——跌幅小于存储，但仍会跌。1,185 亿美元回购是地板，不是盾牌。') }}</td><td>{{ t('The quality rebound vehicle: cleared-out positioning, ~20&ndash;24x forward, Rubin cycle. Trade it; the house view stands.', '优质反弹载具：仓位已出清、前瞻约 20&ndash;24 倍、Rubin 周期。做波段；本台原判定不变。') }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>GOOGL</strong></td><td>{{ t('Quality ballast. Proof printed, dilution behind it, $340&ndash;370 is the accumulation zone.', '优质压舱石。证据已打印、稀释已落地，340&ndash;370 美元是积累区。') }}</td><td>{{ t('Steady compounder to new highs by 2027 — but the explosive rerating already happened.', '2027 年前稳步复利创新高——但爆发式重估已经发生过了。') }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>TSLA</strong></td><td colspan="2">{{ t('Not in this contest. Institutions are net sellers to retail; ~181x forward. Optimus V3 is a separate, option-sized 2027 physical-AI bet — see The Second Act §8.3.', '不在本场选角中。机构在向散户净卖出；前瞻约 181 倍。Optimus V3 属于另一笔期权级的 2027「物理 AI」押注——见《第二幕》§8.3。') }}</td></tr>
</table>

<p>{{ t('Dark horses, for completeness: <strong>MSFT</strong> is the contrarian trough accumulation (worst-performing megacap, cleanest AI-revenue proof); <strong>AMZN</strong> rides at half weight; <strong>AVGO</strong> is the custom-silicon winner wearing semis beta. All three are covered in §5.',
      '补充几匹黑马：<strong>MSFT</strong> 是逆向的低谷建仓标的（表现最差的巨头、AI 收入证据最干净）；<strong>AMZN</strong> 以半权重随行；<strong>AVGO</strong> 是穿着半导体贝塔外衣的自研芯片赢家。三者详见 §5。') }}</p>

<h2 id="twojobs"><span class="num">2</span>{{ t('Two different jobs', '两份不同的工作') }}</h2>

<div class="callout lead"><span class="co-h">{{ t('In plain English', '通俗版') }}</span>
{{ t('&ldquo;Safe haven&rdquo; gets used for two different things: the stock that <em>doesn&rsquo;t go down</em> when everything else does, and the stock that <em>goes up the most</em> once the selling stops. Google in late 2025 did both at once — which is rare, and it&rsquo;s why everyone remembers it. Testing Meta against that memory requires splitting the jobs first.',
     '「避险」这个词其实被用来指两件不同的事：一是在别人都跌时<em>不怎么跌</em>的股票，二是抛售一停就<em>涨得最多</em>的股票。2025 年底的谷歌罕见地同时做到了两者——所以所有人都记得它。要用这段记忆检验 Meta，得先把两份工作拆开。') }}
</div>

<p>{{ t('Job one is <strong>shelter</strong>: absorbing capital on the way down. Its mechanics are boring — low beta, low correlation, a buyback bid under the stock, no financing needs, no binary events on the calendar. Job two is <strong>rerating leadership</strong>: being the name underweight managers are forced to chase once fear breaks. Its mechanics are the opposite — a fresh classification change, cleared-out positioning, and a proof event that turns a discount into a premium. A stock can hold both roles only when its proof event lands <em>during</em> everyone else&rsquo;s drawdown. That is precisely what happened to Google, and precisely what is not yet scheduled for Meta.',
      '第一份工作是<strong>庇护</strong>：在下跌途中吸纳资金。它的机制很无聊——低贝塔、低相关性、股价下方有回购买盘、没有融资需求、日历上没有二元事件。第二份工作是<strong>重估领导权</strong>：当恐惧散去，低配的基金经理被迫追买的那只股票。它的机制恰好相反——全新的类别重划、已被出清的仓位、以及一个把折价变成溢价的证据事件。一只股票只有当它的证据事件恰好落在<em>别人的回撤期间</em>，才能同时担任两个角色。这正是谷歌当时的际遇，也正是 Meta 日历上还没有排上的东西。') }}</p>

<p>{{ t('Our own engines make the split visible right now. The Mag-7 basket is the <em>only</em> basket on the board positive month-to-date (+3.9%) while Memory &amp; HBM bleeds &minus;12.3%<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup> — rotation into perceived quality is already running, exactly the 2018/2000 sequence <a href="report_ai_master_plan.html">The AI Master Plan</a> flagged on July 1. Within that rotation, the tape is discriminating: on QQQ-down days since June 1, Apple beat the index 77% of the time with +1.7% mean excess; Meta beat it 54% with +1.1%; Nvidia beat it 31% with &minus;0.4%; Tesla 38% with &minus;0.7%<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>. The haven vote is not hypothetical — it is being counted daily, and Apple is winning it.',
      '本站引擎已经把这条分界线照了出来。月初至今，Mag-7 是全板块<em>唯一</em>收正的篮子（+3.9%），而存储与 HBM 篮子失血 &minus;12.3%<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>——向「感知中的优质」轮动已在进行，正是<a href="report_ai_master_plan.html">《AI 总体规划》</a>7月1日标记的 2018/2000 序列。而在这轮轮动内部，盘面在做区分：6月1日以来的 QQQ 下跌日中，Apple 以 +1.7% 的平均超额跑赢指数 77% 的时间；Meta 为 54%、+1.1%；Nvidia 为 31%、&minus;0.4%；Tesla 为 38%、&minus;0.7%<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>。避险投票不是假设——它每天都在计票，而 Apple 正在赢。') }}</p>

<h2 id="template"><span class="num">3</span>{{ t('The Google template, measured', '谷歌模板的度量') }}</h2>

<div class="callout lead"><span class="co-h">{{ t('In plain English', '通俗版') }}</span>
{{ t('Before asking whether Meta can repeat Google&rsquo;s move, we measured what the move actually was, from our own price store. Google gained 28% in a quarter where the Nasdaq gained 2%, and it <em>rose</em> 5% while the index fell 8% — the only giant that did. But three things made that possible, and all three were in hand <em>before</em> the quarter started: the court risk was gone, the cloud profits were printed, and Warren Buffett showed up as the seal of approval.',
     '在问 Meta 能否复刻谷歌之前，我们先用本站价格库把那段行情量了一遍。谷歌在纳指只涨 2% 的那个季度里涨了 28%，并在指数下跌 8% 的窗口内<em>逆势上涨</em> 5%——巨头中独一份。但成就这一切的三件事，在季度开始<em>之前</em>就已经到手：法院风险消失、云业务利润已经打印、巴菲特带着认证印章现身。') }}
</div>

