  <figcaption>{{ t('Store-measured totals: GOOGL +27.9% vs QQQ +1.8% over Oct 1&ndash;Dec 31 2025; during QQQ&rsquo;s &minus;7.9% peak-to-trough (Oct 29 &rarr; Nov 20), GOOGL +5.4%, AAPL &minus;1.2%, AMZN &minus;5.7%, AVGO &minus;10.1%, MSFT &minus;11.5%, NVDA &minus;12.8%, META &minus;21.6%. Paths between anchors are schematic. Sources: data/stocks + massive_stock_day parquet stores.',
      '价格库实测总额：2025年10月1日&ndash;12月31日 GOOGL +27.9%、QQQ +1.8%；QQQ 峰谷回撤 &minus;7.9%（10月29日 &rarr; 11月20日）期间，GOOGL +5.4%、AAPL &minus;1.2%、AMZN &minus;5.7%、AVGO &minus;10.1%、MSFT &minus;11.5%、NVDA &minus;12.8%、META &minus;21.6%。锚点之间的路径为示意。来源：data/stocks 与 massive_stock_day 数据库。') }}</figcaption>
</figure>

<p>{{ t('Three details from the measurement matter more than the headline. <strong>First, the haven behavior was inflow-driven, not defensiveness.</strong> On QQQ-down days that quarter, Google beat the index only 55% of the time — <em>less</em> than Microsoft (72%) or Apple (62%)<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>. What made Google the haven was that it kept <em>rising through</em> the drawdown: fresh money was arriving daily, so the dips didn&rsquo;t stick. A haven is made by flows, not by beta. <strong>Second, its beta halved</strong> — from 2.58 to 1.26 in one quarter<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup> — which is what a classification change looks like in the covariance data. <strong>Third, the proof predated the price.</strong> The rerating&rsquo;s catalysts were all disclosure events: the September 2 antitrust ruling that took forced breakup off the table (+9% in a session, ~$234B of market cap<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>), the November 14 Berkshire 13F revealing a $4.9B stake<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>, Gemini 3 on November 18, and a cloud P&amp;L that was already profitable with a $240B printed backlog<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>. The multiple went from ~17x trailing at the March-2025 trough to ~29x by year-end<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup> because each leg of the story was <em>documented</em> before the market paid for it.',
      '度量结果中有三个细节比标题数字更重要。<strong>第一，避险行为是资金流入驱动的，不是防御性。</strong>那个季度 QQQ 的下跌日里，谷歌跑赢指数的比例只有 55%——<em>低于</em>微软（72%）和 Apple（62%）<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>。让谷歌成为避风港的，是它在回撤中持续<em>逆势上行</em>：新钱每天都在进场，下跌根本站不住。避风港由资金流铸成，而非贝塔。<strong>第二，它的贝塔腰斩</strong>——一个季度内从 2.58 降到 1.26<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>——这就是「类别重划」在协方差数据里的模样。<strong>第三，证据先于价格。</strong>那轮重估的催化剂全是披露事件：9月2日反垄断裁决排除强制拆分（单日 +9%、约 2,340 亿美元市值<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>）、11月14日伯克希尔 13F 披露 49 亿美元持仓<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>、11月18日 Gemini 3 发布，以及一个已经盈利、且在手订单 2,400 亿美元已经打印的云业务<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>。估值从 2025 年 3 月低谷的约 17 倍升至年末约 29 倍<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>，因为故事的每一条腿都是先有<em>文件</em>，市场才付钱。') }}</p>

<div class="callout warn"><span class="co-h">{{ t('A correction to the folk memory', '对民间记忆的一处修正') }}</span>
{{ t('The &ldquo;November 2025 Nasdaq correction&rdquo; that Google supposedly sailed through was shallow: S&amp;P 500 &minus;5.7% from its October high, NDX &minus;1.6% for the month, QQQ &minus;7.9% peak-to-trough<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup> — a valuation dip, not a &minus;10% technical correction. One of the external AI briefs we audited also mis-centers Google&rsquo;s rerating on its Q1-2026 results; in fact the Q4-2025 earnings (Feb 4, 2026) <em>fell</em> 3% after hours on the capex guide<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>. The rerate was a Sep&ndash;Dec 2025 disclosure sequence. Getting this right matters: it means the template requires proof <em>before</em> the drawdown, and it was never stress-tested by a real &minus;15% tape. Whoever plays haven this autumn faces a harder exam than Google ever sat.',
      '所谓谷歌安然穿越的「2025年11月纳指调整」其实很浅：标普自10月高点 &minus;5.7%、纳指100当月 &minus;1.6%、QQQ 峰谷 &minus;7.9%<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>——是一次估值回吐，不是 &minus;10% 的技术性调整。我们审计的外部 AI 简报之一还把谷歌的重估错误地锚定在 2026 年一季报上；事实是 2025 年四季报（2026年2月4日）因资本开支指引盘后<em>下跌</em> 3%<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>。那轮重估是 2025 年 9&ndash;12 月的一串披露事件。厘清这一点很重要：它意味着模板要求证据在回撤<em>之前</em>到位，而且它从未经受过真正 &minus;15% 级别行情的压力测试。今秋无论谁来扮演避风港，考卷都比谷歌当年的更难。') }}
</div>

<h2 id="meta"><span class="num">4</span>{{ t('Meta&rsquo;s audition', 'Meta 的试镜') }}</h2>

<div class="callout lead"><span class="co-h">{{ t('In plain English', '通俗版') }}</span>
{{ t('Meta&rsquo;s July was real: a cloud business in the works, a paid AI model, subscriptions rolling out, the stock&rsquo;s best week in years. The rerating story is the strongest of any megacap. But as a <em>shelter</em> for the next three months it fails the checklist on every line: it burned its buyback, it may sell $64B of new stock, its new business has no revenue yet, and last time the index fell hard it was the worst performer of the group. Own it as the recovery trade, sized for violence — not as the bunker.',
     'Meta 的七月是真的：算力云业务在筹备、付费 AI 模型上线、订阅在铺开、股价创多年最佳单周。它的重估故事是所有巨头中最强的。但作为未来三个月的<em>掩体</em>，它在检查表的每一行都不及格：回购烧没了、可能增发 640 亿美元新股、新业务还没有收入，而且上一次指数重挫时它是全组表现最差的。把它当作复苏交易来持有、按剧烈波动定仓——不要当防空洞。') }}
</div>

<p>{{ t('First, what genuinely rhymes with the template. Meta enters this audition <strong>underowned</strong>: our ownership desk has it at &ldquo;low&rdquo; crowding, held by 17 of 51 tracked funds after 13 cut it in Q1, with Tepper&rsquo;s Appaloosa among the trimmers<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup> — the same cleared-out starting point Google had. It enters <strong>discounted</strong>: &minus;23.5% below its August-2025 high of $788 after a &minus;33% derate to the March trough<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>, on roughly 17&ndash;19x the consensus 2027 earnings line<sup class="ev ev-s">S</sup> (consensus figures are single-source this week; treat as indicative). And it has the <strong>freshest classification change</strong> in the market: Meta Compute — reported July 1, Bloomberg — would make it the first hyperscaler to flip from compute <em>buyer</em> to compute <em>seller</em><sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>; Muse Spark 1.1 opened the first paid Meta model API on July 9 at $1.25/$4.25 per million tokens, roughly a quarter of rival list prices<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>; subscriptions began rolling out May 27<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>. The stock answered: +8.8% on July 1 while its own suppliers fell, its best week in years into July 10<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>, and a 20-day beta to QQQ that collapsed from 1.80 in March to ~0.5<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>. The narrative inversion — from &ldquo;ad company overspending on AI&rdquo; to &ldquo;AI platform funded by ads&rdquo; — is underway. On this much, the external briefs and our data agree.',
      '先说与模板真正押韵的部分。Meta 带着<strong>低配仓位</strong>走进试镜：本站持仓台给它的拥挤度评级为「低」，51 家跟踪基金中仅 17 家持有、一季度有 13 家减持，Tepper 的 Appaloosa 也在减持之列<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>——与谷歌当年同样「已被出清」的起点。它带着<strong>折价</strong>：较 2025 年 8 月 788 美元的高点仍低 23.5%，此前一路 &minus;33% 跌到 3 月低谷<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>，对应 2027 年共识盈利约 17&ndash;19 倍<sup class="ev ev-s">S</sup>（本周共识数字为单一来源，仅作参考）。它还握着全市场<strong>最新鲜的类别重划</strong>：Meta Compute——彭博 7月1日报道——将使它成为第一家从算力<em>买家</em>翻转为算力<em>卖家</em>的超大规模厂商<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>；Muse Spark 1.1 于 7月9日开放首个付费 Meta 模型 API，每百万 token 定价 $1.25/$4.25，约为对手报价的四分之一<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>；订阅已于 5月27日开始铺开<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>。股价给出了回应：7月1日 +8.8% 而其供应商齐跌、7月10日收出多年最佳单周<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>、对 QQQ 的20日贝塔从 3 月的 1.80 坍缩到约 0.5<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>。从「烧钱做 AI 的广告公司」到「用广告养 AI 的平台」的叙事翻转已经启动。到这里为止，外部简报与我们的数据是一致的。') }}</p>

<p>{{ t('Now the disqualifiers — not for the trade, but for the <em>haven</em> job. They come in four layers.',
      '接下来是不合格项——不是否定这笔交易，而是否定<em>避险</em>这份工作。共有四层。') }}</p>

<table class="data">
  <tr><th>{{ t('Template requirement', '模板要求') }}</th><th>{{ t('Google, entering Q4 2025', '谷歌，2025年四季度入场时') }}</th><th>{{ t('Meta, entering the fall of 2026', 'Meta，2026年秋入场时') }}</th></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>{{ t('De-risking event', '去风险事件') }}</strong></td><td class="r-pos">{{ t('Done — Sep 2 ruling removed breakup risk', '已完成——9月2日裁决排除拆分风险') }}</td><td class="r-neg">{{ t('Pending — FTC appeal of the dismissed monopoly case is live', '未完成——FTC 对被驳回垄断案的上诉仍在进行') }}<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup></td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>{{ t('Printed proof', '已打印的证据') }}</strong></td><td class="r-pos">{{ t('Profitable cloud, $240B backlog disclosed', '云业务已盈利，在手订单 2,400 亿美元已披露') }}</td><td class="r-neg">{{ t('Meta Compute: no launch date, no pricing, no revenue, no backlog; company declined comment', 'Meta Compute：无上线日期、无定价、无收入、无在手订单；公司拒绝置评') }}<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup></td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>{{ t('Capital mechanics', '资本机制') }}</strong></td><td class="r-pos">{{ t('Buybacks running through the window', '窗口期内回购持续进行') }}</td><td class="r-neg">{{ t('Buybacks $0 in Q1 (vs $12.75B a year ago); ~$64B equity raise under consideration', '一季度回购为 0（去年同期 127.5 亿美元）；约 640 亿美元股权融资在酝酿') }}<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup></td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>{{ t('Validation buyer', '认证买家') }}</strong></td><td class="r-pos">{{ t('Berkshire 13F, Nov 14', '伯克希尔 13F，11月14日') }}</td><td class="r-neg">{{ t('None disclosed; next 13F window is August 14', '尚无披露；下一个 13F 窗口为 8月14日') }}<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup></td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>{{ t('Stress-test record', '压力测试记录') }}</strong></td><td class="r-pos">{{ t('+5.4% through the QQQ drawdown', 'QQQ 回撤期间 +5.4%') }}</td><td class="r-neg">{{ t('&minus;21.6% through the same drawdown — worst of the group', '同一回撤期间 &minus;21.6%——全组最差') }}<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup></td></tr>
</table>

<p>{{ t('<strong>The reflexivity trap is the deepest layer.</strong> Meta&rsquo;s new story is not a hedge against the AI-capex trade — it <em>is</em> the AI-capex trade, restated as a vendor. Management raised the 2026 capex guide to $125&ndash;145B and named memory prices as the driver<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>; the compute it would lease is the same compute whose scarcity pricing the correction would deflate; the neoclouds it would undercut are the canaries of the credit tape. If semis and memory correct because AI-capex credibility cracks — the modal Phase-1 path in <a href="report_ai_master_plan.html">The AI Master Plan</a>, memory &minus;30&ndash;45% from highs — Meta&rsquo;s option on compute resale reprices down <em>with</em> the complex, not against it. <a href="report_second_act.html">The Second Act</a> called Meta &ldquo;the highest-beta platform on this question, in both directions,&rdquo; and July proved the both-directions clause: +8.8% on July 1, &minus;4.9% on July 2<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>. That is the signature of a rerating candidate, and the opposite of a shelter&rsquo;s.',
      '<strong>反身性陷阱是最深的一层。</strong>Meta 的新故事不是对 AI 资本开支交易的对冲——它<em>就是</em>那笔交易本身，只是换成了卖方的说法。管理层把 2026 年资本开支指引上调至 1,250&ndash;1,450 亿美元，点名存储器价格是主因<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>；它要出租的算力，正是这轮调整将会压缩其稀缺定价的那批算力；它要降价打击的新兴云，正是信用行情的金丝雀。如果半导体与存储因 AI 资本开支可信度破裂而调整——即<a href="report_ai_master_plan.html">《AI 总体规划》</a>阶段一的众数路径，存储自高点 &minus;30&ndash;45%——Meta 的算力转售期权将与板块<em>同向</em>下修，而非反向。<a href="report_second_act.html">《第二幕》</a>称 Meta 为「在这个问题上双向弹性最高的平台」，而七月验证了「双向」二字：7月1日 +8.8%，7月2日 &minus;4.9%<sup class="ev ev-f">F</sup>。这是重估候选人的签名，恰是掩体的反面。') }}</p>

<p>{{ t('<strong>July 29 is a binary, not a checkpoint.</strong> Q2 earnings land after the close that day<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>. The bull needs: revenue near the top of the $58&ndash;61B guide, the 2026 operating-income commitment defended, capex <em>held</em>, and any concrete Meta Compute or subscription disclosure. The bear needs only one sentence: a third capex raise with no revenue attached — or confirmation of the equity raise into a weak tape. Note also what Zuckerberg told an internal town hall on July 2: AI-agent progress &ldquo;hasn&rsquo;t really accelerated in the way that we expected&rdquo;<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup> — the model-quality leg of this story is not yet load-bearing. Our read: the probability-weighted outcome of the print is negative for the haven framing and constructive for the entry framing. A post-earnings selldown is tranche one of the house buy-list, already on the books in <a href="report_relapse_jul8.html">The Relapse</a>; the dilution event, if it comes, marks the low&rsquo;s neighborhood, not the thesis&rsquo;s death.',
      '<strong>7月29日是二元事件，不是例行检查点。</strong>二季报当日盘后发布<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>。多头需要：收入贴近 580&ndash;610 亿美元指引上限、守住 2026 年营业利润承诺、资本开支<em>按兵不动</em>、外加任何一条具体的 Meta Compute 或订阅披露。空头只需要一句话：第三次上调资本开支而不附带收入——或在弱势盘面中确认股权融资。还要注意扎克伯格 7月2日在内部全员会上的话：AI 智能体的进展「并没有像我们预期的那样加速」<sup class="ev ev-c">C</sup>——这个故事里「模型质量」这条腿尚未承重。我们的判读：这份财报按概率加权的结果，对「避险」叙事是负面的，对「入场」叙事是建设性的。财报后的下杀正是本台买入清单的第一批——<a href="report_relapse_jul8.html">《复燃》</a>已经记账；而稀释事件若发生，标记的是低点的街区，不是论点的死亡。') }}</p>

